From e69fd94a7d19e297277fd51c422dcd4d8243345c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaron Shahrabani <EMAIL>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:10:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: Flush the CTL before enabling the video timing
 engine

Since commit f9cb8d8d836e ("drm/msm/mdp5: rework CTL START signal
handling") a full modeset defers the CTL flush of the pipes and mixers
from mdp5_crtc_atomic_flush() to encoder->enable(). For video mode,
mdp5_vid_encoder_enable() enables the INTF timing engine first and
writes CTL_FLUSH afterwards, so the double-buffered pipe and mixer
registers only latch at the end of the first frame. That frame is
fetched with whatever the pipes held before the CRTC was disabled.

On MSM8916 (Samsung Galaxy Tab A 9.7, SM-T550, DSI video mode panel)
this shows up at most DPMS on transitions: the compositor (phoc) has
freed the buffer it scanned out before the blank, so the MDP reads an
unmapped iova and the commit times out:

  qcom-iommu-ctx 1e24000.iommu-ctx: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x40000202, iova=0x0000000000602000, fsynr=0x23, cb=4
  msm_mdp 1a01000.display-controller: vblank time out, crtc=0
  [drm:mdp5_irq_error_handler [msm]] *ERROR* errors: 04000000

The faulting iova is always the start of the framebuffer that was
displayed before the blank. The same ordering also produces an INTF1
underrun on every boot, when the first modeset takes over the
bootloader's pipe setup.

Write the flush before starting the timing engine, as DPU does.

Testing, all on SM-T550 with the msm8916-mainline 7.3-rc2 tree: the
same sequence of 22 DPMS off/on cycles after a fresh boot logged 37
context faults (rate limited), 2 vblank timeouts and 9 underruns
without this patch, and none with it; the boot-time underrun is gone
as well. Not tested on mainline itself: msm8916-mainline additionally
calls the MDP5 encoder's enable after the DSI bridge chain, which does
not change the ordering inside mdp5_vid_encoder_enable(). Command mode
and writeback are not affected by the change and were not tested.

Fixes: f9cb8d8d836e ("drm/msm/mdp5: rework CTL START signal handling")
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
index eaba3b2..1617aea 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
@@ -164,10 +164,17 @@ static void mdp5_vid_encoder_enable(struct drm_encoder *encoder)
 	if (WARN_ON(mdp5_encoder->enabled))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Flush before starting the timing engine: on a full modeset the
+	 * pipe and mixer flush was deferred to here, and a flush written
+	 * after the timing engine started only latches at the end of the
+	 * first frame, which is then fetched with the pre-disable state.
+	 */
+	mdp5_ctl_commit(ctl, pipeline, mdp_ctl_flush_mask_encoder(intf), true);
+
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&mdp5_encoder->intf_lock, flags);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_TIMING_ENGINE_EN(intfn), 1);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mdp5_encoder->intf_lock, flags);
-	mdp5_ctl_commit(ctl, pipeline, mdp_ctl_flush_mask_encoder(intf), true);
 
 	mdp5_ctl_set_encoder_state(ctl, pipeline, true);
 
